                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df135637-2dd7-3607-bd46-814ae75ea5cb",
                        "entry_id": "c4c87acd-50e4-3eb5-902d-77ccb3ad4234",
                        "glosses": [
                            "taki, który da się sprawdzić, możliwy do weryfikacji"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6a7893d-5b34-462b-9d97-2f5da452a55e",
                                "sense_id": "df135637-2dd7-3607-bd46-814ae75ea5cb",
                                "text": "W estetyce Przybosia dwa są tereny sprawdzalne, odwoławcze: poezja i malarstwo"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b0bc61a-77e7-4038-9fb2-5ecb58ec614f",
                                "sense_id": "df135637-2dd7-3607-bd46-814ae75ea5cb",
                                "text": "Autor tekstu, Roman Adler, stawia odważne hipotezy, co ciekawe, sprawdzalne"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a98d33d-9187-42cd-82bf-105a86b6976e",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4c87acd-50e4-3eb5-902d-77ccb3ad4234",
                        "source_sense_id": "df135637-2dd7-3607-bd46-814ae75ea5cb",
                        "target_lang_word": "verifiable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "verifiable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e01bc505-369b-37d4-ba49-2ac15f2f6b00",
                                        "entry_id": "8525c203-71b7-3a30-befc-5b3c176bfdbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be verified or confirmed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a443852f-b5b6-44a4-bf67-089b70259ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "e01bc505-369b-37d4-ba49-2ac15f2f6b00",
                                                "text": "Do you have verifiable evidence to support that claim?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8320eac5-e0bb-475a-8b57-2c808a8b122e",
                                                "sense_id": "e01bc505-369b-37d4-ba49-2ac15f2f6b00",
                                                "text": "Sometimes these sagas and anecdotes are touched with ribaldry, or with excessive obscenity, according to the times, and sometimes they are rooted in obscure but still verifiable deistic concepts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3804487-a747-44f7-99c9-2e8a9f27a2c2",
                                                "sense_id": "e01bc505-369b-37d4-ba49-2ac15f2f6b00",
                                                "text": "But the post-truthism that the new autocrats are so apt at employing goes far beyond fibbing: it denies the existence of a verifiable reality. Post-truthism is not chiefly about getting lies accepted as truths but about muddying the waters to the point that it becomes difficult to discern the difference between truth and falsehood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc61d8d3-9810-37ef-9ff4-d6abf6f87a99",
                                        "entry_id": "8525c203-71b7-3a30-befc-5b3c176bfdbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be qualified by a Boolean expression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "verifiable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4878906e-d853-398a-aa36-53f26b57203f",
                                        "entry_id": "9d227c2f-d49a-3bdf-bc1f-51ab4f4f4940",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A statement or observation that can be verified."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ff5aeb2-3e55-4add-a43d-44c70867a8f6",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4c87acd-50e4-3eb5-902d-77ccb3ad4234",
                        "source_sense_id": "df135637-2dd7-3607-bd46-814ae75ea5cb",
